/*****************************************************************************
    jitThenT -- the REGRESSION NET for jitEmitGIF's then arm, 2026-07-31.
    Sibling of incant/jitElseT, which carries the actual POP and the full story.

    Same fixture, true condition:

        testIfElse code={ if righty > 0; maximus = righty * 2; else maximus = 7; }

        righty = 13  ->  maximus = 26    THEN arm reached
                         maximus = 7     would mean the else arm ran
                         maximus = 11    would mean neither ran

    ⚠ THIS ROW IS NOT EVIDENCE THAT THE ELSE ARM WORKS, and it never was. It
    was green BEFORE the else arm existed, because it exercises only the arm
    that was being emitted -- correct by luck. Its job is the opposite: to catch
    the else-arm change BREAKING the path that already worked. Read it as a net,
    not as a proof.

    ⚠⚠ SEPARATE FILE FROM jitElseT ON PURPOSE -- ONE `testing()` PER RUN. A
    second generate on the same action in one process hits the sequential-state-
    corruption tar baby and reports a regression that does not exist. See
    jitElseT's header; it paid for that lesson.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

righty  = 13;
maximus = 11;
print "then-arm setup : righty =" righty " maximus =" maximus:;
testing(testIfElse);
print "then-arm result: maximus =" maximus " (want 26; 7 = wrong arm; 11 = neither)":;

print "JT SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
